      "problem": "| $f$ | $Y=-2$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.16$ | $0.09$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.44$ | $0.21$ | $0.05$ |\n\nThe joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above, while the marginal mass functions for these variables are shown below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">${f}_{X}(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.7$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n<p></p><p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">${f}_{Y}(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n<p></p><p></p></th></tr></tbody></table>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $P(X=0,Y=0)=P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=0)$\n\nII. $P(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$\n\nIII. $X$ and $Y$ are independent",
